ts  they have great teeth most people in my  family uh went the  doctor dentist route aside from me and  my brother  but they're like i want to say like 10  dentists in the family  it was definitely um the  path less chosen being a chef no one in  my family  really was a professional cook my  grandmother  was a home economics teacher so i guess  that's kind of  maybe where i got you know the cooking  bug  why southeast asian cuisine for you i  just  found the food so fascinating and the  flavors  so bold and uh intimidating at the same  time  i felt connected to that part of the  world  i like the way you talk about breakfast  in the book yeah and that it's such a  different there's  breakfast such a different concept in  southeast asia than it is here  there are not specific dishes that you  would necessarily  eat just for breakfast like we think of  cereal and all that stuff  but in the philippines for example they  eat like rice dried fish  soup there is no real rules necessarily  for breakfast although i tried to make  more breakfasty brunchy items for that  chapter  also in the book lumpia shanghai olympia  olympia yeah and i'm dipping this in  this is a sweet chili sauce so it's a  little sweet  savory it's not spicy at all  perfect thank you and the bangkok  fire made with chili-infused whiskey  cheers  cheers  oh yeah that does have heat but for the  moment  back to the coconuts when you pick one  you want it to  feel heavy that means that there is a  lot of liquid inside and that will  make more coconut milk coconut milk  sounded great to us  so cohen i think you can do it let us  take a whack at it yeah  perfect you're a pro look at that see  it felt aggressive yeah it's a good way  to get your anger out i think  in a good way yeah totally it's  therapeutic you know  that may be something we all need in  these times  cohen's restaurant in new york city pig  and cow  is open during the pandemic but for  takeout only  she hopes her cookbook will inspire  people to make some outside of the box  creations at home that they might not  try otherwise  though for cohen this accomplishment is  bittersweet  i was really struck by the dedication in  your book  yeah so unfortunately um  in april i lost my father to covid  and so i was able just in time to change  my dedication because originally it was  dedicated to my son  but my father was my biggest fan  and so i wanted to make sure that  everyone knew  um how proud i was of him just like they  knew how proud he was of me  so can you talk about his unconditional  love yeah he was  probably the most positive person i've  ever met  he like knew the secret to life he  really just enjoyed life he knew how to  push people  to do great things without being overly  annoying and on top of you  i love the way she talked about her dad  yeah yeah yeah you were choked up too  i i was i mean it it it's emotional um  and  we thank her for talking about all of  that and we thank her  for the coconut lesson i mean he didn't  bring us i  chili-infused whiskey yeah spicy good  we'll have some after the show

